From c46eb94cc7cf3be2cf3be9b452c67c997a9f187e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:11:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Seccomp: emulate Syscall User Dispatch

prctl(PR_SET_SYSCALL_USER_DISPATCH) was forwarded to the host kernel. On an
Arm64 host without it the guest gets EINVAL; on one with it the host would
dispatch FEX's own syscalls. Wine 11 traps raw syscalls from Windows code
(Denuvo Anti-Cheat, NtContinue loops) only through Syscall User Dispatch, so
under FEX those syscalls ran as Linux syscalls.

Emulate it per thread like Linux's syscall_user_dispatch(): checked before the
seccomp filters, selector byte read fault-safe (SIGSEGV exit on fault, SIGSYS
exit on a bad value), SIGSYS with si_code SYS_USER_DISPATCH delivered through
the same path as SECCOMP_RET_TRAP. Cleared on clone/fork, gone after execve.
Costs one branch per syscall when unused. Upstream FEX main (741e146) has no
support either.

eac-tests/sigsys-redirect: Wine's sigsys_handler redirect + NtContinue context
switch, 200000 traps per phase (SUD, seccomp, sigaltstack, no-sigreturn
escape, nested, 4 threads), native x86-64 oracle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
